llowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pikax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pikax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pikax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pikax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pikax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pikax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pikax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pikax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-04-20T09:16:55Z","updated_at":"2020-04-20T09:39:32Z","body":"As far as I know when you return render function from setup, it will re-render every time creating a new component, but you can simulate the render by creating the render blocks your self [here](https://codesandbox.io/s/jolly-payne-gm0em?file=/index.html)\r\n\r\n```ts\r\n// NOTE HACK\r\n\r\n  const App = {\r\n    setup() {\r\n      const position = ref(new THREE.Vector3(-1, 1, 0));\r\n      setInterval(() => {\r\n        position.value = new THREE.Vector3(Math.random(), 1, 0);\r\n      }, 1000);\r\n\r\n      return {\r\n        position\r\n      };\r\n    },\r\n    render(_ctx, _cache) {\r\n      return (\r\n        openBlock(),\r\n        createBlock(Box, { position: _ctx.pos }, null, 8 /* PROPS */, [\r\n          \"position\"\r\n        ])\r\n      );\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vuejs/core/issues/comments/616420373/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pikax","id":4620458,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjA0NTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4620458?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pikax","html_url":"https://github.com/pikax","followe